🧩 Cloud Infrastructure Components

Cloud infrastructure is composed of interconnected resources that work together to provide computing services.

💻 Compute

Provides the processing power required to run applications, services, and workloads.

💾 Storage

Provides space for operating systems, application files, user data, and other information.

🌐 Networking

Provides communication between users, servers, applications, and other infrastructure resources.

🔐 Identity & Access Management

Controls who can access cloud resources and what actions they are authorized to perform.

🐧 Operating System

Provides the software environment required to manage hardware resources and execute applications.

These components work together rather than functioning as isolated resources. Understanding their relationships is an important part of planning cloud infrastructure.

